# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public-release guards. Do not remove without a disclosure review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Geospatial data is never committed. You supply it at run time — see DATA.md.
# The Barbados Geoportal layers are not ours to redistribute.
bbd-geo-portal/

# `blender/` is a WORKING DIRECTORY, not source. Everything the pipeline writes
# into it is (a) regenerable with `ulap-scope preprocess / build / export /
# coverage` and (b) derived from the geoportal layers above — the manifest and
# the meshes carry the same 576 building footprints and LiDAR heights as the
# shapefiles do. Committing them would route around the guard, so they stay
# local. Tracked here: the pipeline notes and the two render helpers only.
blender/scene_build/
blender/mitsuba_scene/
blender/mitsuba_scene_terrain/
blender/sionna_out/
blender/*.tif
blender/*.wld
# Superseded by ulap-scope/ulap_scope/stages/ — the packaged copies are portable
# (env-var driven); these local ones hard-coded a developer's home directory.
blender/build_scene.py
blender/clip_study_area.py
blender/export_mitsuba.py
blender/fetch_basemap.py
blender/preprocess_scene.py
blender/sionna_analysis.py
blender/sionna_animate_rx.py
blender/sionna_coverage.py
blender/sionna_mmwave_sinr.py
blender/sionna_terrain_ground.py

# Internal brand, positioning, and go-to-market material. Not for public release.
brandkit/

# Paper sources live in the separate papers repository. This tree keeps only
# research-paper/README.md, the published-papers index.
research-paper/*
!research-paper/README.md

# Credentials — belt and braces. Nothing of the sort has ever been committed
# (verified with gitleaks over full history); keep it that way.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*service-account*.json
credentials*.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
